 "whatThisIs": "A CMS article page (id 1899, https://thalasses.com/en/article/1899) titled \"Sitting outdoor area\". Its own content is: an H1, a one-line strapline rendered in an <h6 class=\"block-title\"> (\"Enjoy your dinner in the outdoor sitting area which provides you a gas barbecue station, as well.\") that is reused verbatim as the meta/og/twitter description, one further sentence in a <p> (\"Daily breakfast can be arranged for our guests!\"), and a fancybox photo album of 58 images whose alt attributes are all generic CMS labels (\"Album Image  #NNNNN\") with empty data-caption attributes. Its meta keywords string is \"Thalasses Villas,Sitting outdoor area,Amenities,Rethymno,Greece,Properties chain\", so the CMS files it under Amenities, not Experiences. On the homepage it is linked as <a href=\"article/1899-1.html\"> from inside the \"Amenities\" section (the block opened by <div id=\"category571\">), as a card labelled \"Sitting outdoor area\" sitting alongside \"Private Beach\" and \"Playground and vegetable garden\". Everything else on the page is site-wide chrome: nav, booking bar, newsletter, footer and the full terms and conditions text.",
 "todos": [
